course: dictionary
lesson: 13540
title: Words that name an impossibility
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impossible is an adjective: it describes something that cannot happen. Add -ity and you get a noun, impossibility, which names that state. «Rolling a 7 on a normal six-sided dice is an impossibility.» Here the word names the idea that a 7 cannot come up on that dice.
explain: You can use the noun to name the thing itself as well. «Lifting a whole elephant with one finger is a physical impossibility.» Physical tells you the problem is about the body and the real world, not about ideas.
explain: Use the context to check. Ask: what cannot happen here? In «It is a logical impossibility for a circle to be square», the clue is that the words contradict each other, so the impossibility is in the logic.
fact: Impossibility is the state of being impossible: something that cannot happen or cannot be done.
fact: An impossibility is a thing that cannot happen.
fact: Impossible becomes impossibility when you add -ity and change the y to i.
fact: In probability, an impossible event has a probability of 0. «Rolling a 7 on a normal dice» is an example.
fact: A logical impossibility contradicts itself, like «a square circle». A near impossibility is almost impossible, but not quite.
exercise: «Rolling a 7 on a normal six-sided dice is an impossibility.» What is an impossibility here? | Something that is very slow | Something that happens every day | A kind of game played with dice | *Something that cannot happen
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Lifting a whole elephant with one finger is a physical impossibility.» that names the state of being impossible. | *impossibility | lifting | finger | physical
exercise: In a probability lesson, an impossible event has a probability of what? | 1 | 50 | 6 | *0
test: «It is a logical impossibility for a circle to be square.» What does logical impossibility mean? | A shape with four sides | *Something that contradicts itself, like a square circle | Something that is very heavy | Something that is very easy to do
test: «Climbing that wall was a near impossibility for Sam.» What does near impossibility mean? | Something that is always easy | Something that happens only at night | *Something that is almost impossible | A kind of wall
exam: «The hero faced a near impossibility: a race against time with no map.» What is a near impossibility? | A quick race with friends | A type of map | *Something that is almost impossible to do | Something very easy
